From Manuel.Eugster at stat.uni-muenchen.de  Sun Aug 23 09:39:59 2009
From: Manuel.Eugster at stat.uni-muenchen.de (Manuel J. A. Eugster)
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2009 09:39:59 +0200
Subject: [Roxygen-devel] roxygen and subclassing? - Error in
	cdr(preorder.flatten.expression(expression))
In-Reply-To: <C1042DFE616D09488C393EF0C384C0C52F0F826801@petex01.prbo.org>
References: <C1042DFE616D09488C393EF0C384C0C52F0F826801@petex01.prbo.org>
Message-ID: <4A90F24F.6050807@stat.uni-muenchen.de>

Hi Mark,

in case of S4 you have to specify the classes, methods, etc in
"full style", e.g.,

setClass("BClass",
   contains=c("BClass"),
   representation=representation(
     s1="character",
     s2="numeric"))

That's because the Roxygen parser is very rudimentary in case of
S4.


Best,

Manuel.



